hadiths[31]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17240","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, he said: Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from Bushayr ibn Ka'b, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The master of seeking forgiveness is that the servant says: O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me and I am Your servant, and I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I can, I acknowledge to You the blessing and I acknowledge to You my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You, he said: If he says it after morning, certain of it, then dies, he is of the people of Paradise, and if he says it after evening, certain of it, then dies, he is of the people of Paradise."
"17241","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad ibn Aws, that he passed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at the time of the Conquest, by a man cupping at al-Baqi' when eighteen had passed of Ramadan, while he was holding my hand, and said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"17242","Isma'il narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: Two things I memorized from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Allah Almighty has prescribed excellence upon everything, so when you kill, excel in killing, and when you slaughter, excel in slaughtering, and let one of you sharpen his blade and rest his slaughtered animal."
"17243","Rawh narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyya, he said: Shaddad ibn Aws was on a journey and alighted at a lodging, and said to his servant: Bring us the blade to play with it, so I disapproved of him, and he said: I have not spoken a word since I became Muslim except that I bridle and restrain it, except this word of mine, so do not preserve it against me, and preserve from me what I say to you: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When people hoard gold and silver, hoard these words: O Allah, I ask You firmness in the affair and resolve upon guidance, and I ask You gratitude for Your blessing, and I ask You excellent worship of You, and I ask You a sound heart, and I ask You a truthful tongue, and I ask You of the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know, indeed You are the Knower of the unseen."
"17244","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed me, Ayyub informed me, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah Almighty folded the earth for me until I saw its easts and its wests, and the dominion of my nation will reach what was folded for me of it, and I was given the two treasures, the white and the red, and I asked my Lord Almighty not to destroy my nation by a general famine, and not to set over them an enemy to destroy them generally, and not to clothe them in sects nor make some taste the violence of others, and He said: O Muhammad, when I decree a decree it is not repelled, and I have given you for your nation that I will not destroy them by a general famine, nor set over them an enemy besides themselves to destroy them generally, until some of them destroy others, and some kill others, and some enslave others."
"17245","He said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And I fear for my nation only the misleading Imams, so when the sword is placed in my nation it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection."
"17246","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, two things, that he said: Allah Almighty has prescribed excellence upon everything, so when you kill, excel in killing, and when you slaughter, excel in slaughtering, and let one of you sharpen his blade, then let him rest his slaughtered animal."
"17247","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Abu Asma, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"17248","Haytham ibn Kharija narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Dawud al-San'ani, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, that he went early to the mosque of Damascus, hastening in going, and met Shaddad ibn Aws with al-Sunabihi with him, so I said: Where do you intend, may Allah have mercy on you? They said: We intend here to a sick brother to visit him, so I went with them until they entered upon that man, and said to him: How have you become? He said: I have become with blessing, so Shaddad said to him: Glad tidings of expiations of evils and removal of sins, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Allah Almighty says: When I afflict a believing servant of Mine and he praises Me for what I afflicted him with, he rises from that bed as on the day his mother bore him, free of sins, and the Lord Almighty says: I restrained My servant and afflicted him, so record for him as you used to record for him while he was healthy."
"17249","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Zayd Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: I passed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when eighteen nights had passed of Ramadan, and he saw a man cupping, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"17250","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd narrated to me, Ubada ibn Nusayy informed us, from Shaddad ibn Aws, that he wept, so it was said to him: What makes you weep? He said: Something I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, and I remembered it and it made me weep: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: I fear for my nation shirk and hidden desire, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will your nation associate after you? He said: Yes, indeed they will not worship a sun nor a moon nor a stone nor an idol, but they will show off in their deeds, and hidden desire is that one of them wakes fasting, then a desire of his desires presents itself to him, so he abandons his fast."
"17251","al-Hakam ibn Nafi' Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Dawud, from Ya'la ibn Shaddad, he said: My father Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to me, with Ubada ibn al-Samit present confirming him, he said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Is there among you a stranger, meaning the People of the Book? So we said: No, O Messenger of Allah, so he ordered the door closed and said: Raise your hands and say: There is no god but Allah, so we raised our hands a while, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, put his hand down, then said: Praise be to Allah, O Allah, You sent me with this word and commanded me with it and promised me Paradise for it, and You do not break the promise, then he said: Glad tidings, for Allah Almighty has forgiven you."
"17252","al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Dawud, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There will be after me Imams who kill the prayer from its times, so pray the prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them supererogatory."
"17253","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam informed us, from Damra ibn Habib, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The shrewd is one who subdues himself and works for what is after death, and the incapable is one who makes himself follow his desire and wishes upon Allah."
"17254","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on one of the roads of Madina when eighteen of Ramadan had passed, while he was holding my hand, he passed by a man cupping, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"17255","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Abu al-Ala, meaning al-Qassab, narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Abu Asma, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Madina, he said: And that was when eighteen of Ramadan had passed, and he saw a man cupping, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"17256","He said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a man cupping in Ramadan and said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"17257","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"17258","Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah Almighty has prescribed excellence upon everything, so when you kill, excel in killing, and when you slaughter, excel in slaughtering, and let one of you sharpen his blade and rest his slaughtered animal."
"17259","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abd Allah ibn Zayd, who is Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me while I was cupping when eighteen of Ramadan had passed, and said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"17260","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, Husayn, meaning al-Mu'allim, narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from Bushayr ibn Ka'b, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The master of seeking forgiveness: O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me and I am Your servant, and I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I can, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, I acknowledge to You Your blessing upon me and I acknowledge to You my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You, he said: Whoever says it after morning, certain of it, and dies that day, is of the people of Paradise, and whoever says it after evening, certain of it, and dies that night, is of the people of Paradise."
"17261","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Ibn Burayda, he said: Bushayr ibn Ka'b al-Adawi narrated to me that Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The master of seeking forgiveness, then he mentioned the hadith."
"17262","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from al-Hanzali, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No man goes to his bed and recites a sura of the Book of Allah Almighty but that Allah Almighty sends to him an angel guarding him from everything that harms him until he wakes, whenever he wakes."
"17263","He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to teach us words to supplicate with in our prayer, or he said: at the end of our prayer: O Allah, I ask You firmness in the affair, and I ask You resolve in guidance, and I ask You gratitude for Your blessing and excellent worship of You, and I ask You a sound heart and a truthful tongue, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know, and I ask You of the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know."
"17264","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Qaza'a ibn Suwayd al-Bahili informed us, from Asim ibn Makhlad, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, my father said: al-Ashyab narrated to us and said: from Abu Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever composes a house of poetry after the last Isha, his prayer that night will not be accepted."
"17265","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid, meaning Ibn Bahram, narrated to us, he said: Shahr, meaning Ibn Hawshab, narrated to us, Ibn Ghanm narrated to me that Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to him from the hadith of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The evil of this nation will surely follow the ways of those before them, the People of the Book, step for step like the feather of an arrow to its fellow."
"17266","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Qaza'a narrated to us, Humayd al-A'raj narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you attend your dead, close the eyes, for sight follows the soul, and speak good, for it is secured upon what the family of the deceased says."
"17267","Hasan al-Ashyab narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: Shaddad ibn Aws said: Abu Dharr used to hear a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, containing strictness, then go out to his people, submitting, perhaps stressing upon them, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would later license concerning it, but Abu Dharr would not hear it, so Abu Dharr would cling to the strict command."
"17268","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from one who narrated to him, from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon a man cupping at al-Baqi' when eighteen had passed of Ramadan, while he was holding my hand, and said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"17269","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: Two things I memorized from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Allah has prescribed excellence upon everything, so when you kill, excel in killing, and when you slaughter, excel in slaughtering, and let one of you sharpen his blade and rest his slaughtered animal."
"17270","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid, meaning Ibn Bahram, narrated to us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab said, Ibn Ghanm said: When we entered the mosque of al-Jabiya, I and Abu al-Darda, we met Ubada ibn al-Samit, so he took my right with his left and Abu al-Darda's left with his right, and went walking between us while we were conversing privately, and Allah knows about what we were conversing, and that is his saying, then Ubada ibn al-Samit said: If the life of one of you or both of you is prolonged, you will soon see a man from the midst of the Muslims, meaning from the middle, reciting the Qur'an upon the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, repeating and proclaiming it, declaring its lawful lawful and its unlawful unlawful and abiding by its stations, or reading it upon the tongue of his brother, a reading upon the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, repeating and proclaiming it, declaring its lawful lawful and its unlawful unlawful and abiding by its stations, not turning among you except as the head of a dead donkey turns, he said: While we were thus, Shaddad ibn Aws and Awf ibn Malik appeared and sat with us, so Shaddad said: The most fearful of what I fear for you, O people, is what I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, of hidden desire and shirk, so Ubada ibn al-Samit and Abu al-Darda said: O Allah, forgiveness, had not the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us that Satan has despaired of being worshiped in the Arabian Peninsula? As for hidden desire we have known it, it is the desires of this world of its women and its lusts, so what is this shirk you frighten us with, O Shaddad? So Shaddad said: Have you considered, if you saw a man praying for a man, or fasting for him, or giving charity for him, do you see that he has associated? They said: Yes, by Allah, whoever prays for a man or fasts for him or gives charity for him has associated, so Shaddad said: For I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever prays showing off has associated, and whoever fasts showing off has associated, and whoever gives charity showing off has associated, so Awf ibn Malik said thereupon: Will He not take of all that deed what His Face was sought in it, accepting what was sincere for Him and leaving what was associated with Him? So Shaddad said thereupon: For I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Allah Almighty says: I am the best partner for whoever associates with Me, whoever associates with Me anything, his deed, little and much, is for his partner whom he associated with Me, and I am free of him."
